    "business_profile": "The client is a small-scale Indian enterprise operating under the GST Composition Scheme, as indicated by the utilization of regional accounting terms like \"Kasar A/c\" (used for minor cash discounts or rounding off) and composition tax expense ledgers. Based on the lack of operational creditors and the presence of a single customer named \"Test,\" the entity is likely in a testing, pre-operational, or newly established phase. The client's top customer (debtor) is explicitly listed as Test, while there are no detected top suppliers (creditors) or active bank accounts recorded in the current dataset. The business's financial activities are primarily administrative and regulatory, with its most common expenses identified as Composition(SGST) Tax Exp. A/c, Composition(CGST) Tax Exp. A/c, Interest Expense A/c.(Default), Penalty Expense A/c.(Default), Late Fee Expense A/c.(Default), Other Expense A/c.(Default), and Kasar A/c. To manage its statutory obligations, the business actively utilizes the following tax ledgers: Cash Ledger(CGST) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(SGST) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(IGST) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(CGST- Interest) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(SGST- Interest) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(IGST- Interest) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(CGST- Penalty) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(SGST- Penalty) - Primary Unit, Cash Ledger(IGST- Penalty) - Primary Unit, and Cash Ledger(CGST- Late Fee) - Primary Unit.",
    "specifications": "### **PARSING & MAPPING RULES**\n\n#### **1. Narration Parsing Logic**\n*   **UPI Transaction Rule:** Identify the final segment after the last hyphen (\"-\"). \n    *   If the segment contains a specific remark (e.g., \"FUEL\", \"ICE CREAM\"), use it for categorization.\n    *   If the segment is generic (e.g., \"UPI\", transaction number), revert to the first/second elements to extract the Merchant/Person name.\n*   **NEFT/Other:** Process based on the full text string.\n\n#### **2. Accounting Entry Logic**\n*   **Withdrawal (Outflow):** Debit Ledger | Credit Bank.\n*   **Deposit (Inflow):** Credit Ledger | Debit Bank.\n\n#### **3. Categorization Mappings**\n\n| Keywords (Narration) | Ledger Account | Accounting Group |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| \"GNWEBSOFT PRIVATE LIMITED\" | Salary Account | Direct Income |\n| \"INTEREST PAID TILL\", \"SAVINGS INT\" | Bank Interest Received | Indirect Income (80TTA) |\n| \"DIV\", \"ZEEENT FNLDIV\" | Dividend Income | Indirect Income |\n| \"MONEYLICIOUS\", \"ZERODHA\", \"GROWW\" | Stock/Mutual Fund Investments | Investments (Capital Assets) |\n| \"IPO\", \"DPS IPO\" | IPO Applications | Investments (Capital Assets) |\n| \"LIC\", \"PPF\", \"ELSS\" | Tax Saving Investments | Investments (Section 80C) |\n| \"HEALTH INS\", \"MEDICLAIM\" | Health Insurance Premium | Indirect Expenses (Section 80D) |\n| \"FUEL\", \"PETROLIUM\", \"HP AUTO\", \"MARUTI\" | Petrol & Fuel Expense | Indirect Expenses / Drawings |\n| \"RECHARGE\", \"JIO\", \"AIRTEL\" | Mobile & Internet Expenses | Indirect Expenses / Drawings |\n| \"ICE CREAM\", \"DOSA\", \"HOTEL\", \"CAKE\", \"PUFF\" | Food & Beverages | Indirect Expenses / Drawings |\n| \"INSTAALERTCHG\", \"SMS\" | Bank Charges | Indirect Expenses |\n| \"CARS24\" | Vehicle Expenses/Asset | Fixed Assets / Drawings |\n| \"ATW\", \"ATM\" | Cash In Hand | Cash Account (Contra) |\n\n#### **4. Person-to-Person (P2P) Rules**\n*   **Condition:** If narration contains a person's name AND no expense keyword is present:\n    *   **Withdrawal (Money Sent):** Ledger: [Person's Name] | Group: Loans & Advances OR Personal Drawings.\n    *   **Deposit (Money Received):** Ledger: [Person's Name] | Group: Unsecured Loans OR Loans & Advances (Recovery).\n\n#### **5. Output Format Requirement**\nEvery transaction analysis must strictly follow this structure:\n`Date | Narration | Type (Withdrawal/Deposit) | Amount | Ledger Account | Accounting Group`"
